id: deep-space
name: Deep Space
kind: high
highRank: 4
noWeather: true
unbreathable: true
grantsKnockback: true
knockbackMight: 2
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The deep. Nothing to breathe, no Weather, and every attack throws - 2(bT) further if
  it already did.
text: >
  Deep Space Environment: No air. No Battle Weather. Final destination.

  Hardness Rank: N/A

  Effects: This Battle Environment has multiple effects:

  * This is an Unbreathable Environment.

  * Battle Weather cannot exist in this Battle Environment.

  * All Attacking Maneuvers possess the Knockback Advantage in this Environment. If an
  Attacking Maneuver already possesses the Knockback Advantage, increase your Might by
  2(bT) for the Might Clash initiated by the Knockback Advantage and for calculating the
  number of Squares the target(s) of that Attacking Maneuver are moved.

---

# Local Space with the number doubled, and the fourth rank the frame said "functions
# differently". Whatever that difference is, it is not in these three effects: they are
# Local Space's with 2(bT) where it has 1(bT).
#
# So nothing here treats it as anything but the highest of the four, and the note on the
# rank still says the rules have not said how it differs.
#
# "No air. No Battle Weather. Final destination." Three sentences, three headers:
# `unbreathable`, `noWeather`, and the one that is a joke about a fighting game.
